  "supportTitle": "Support Development",
  "supportDescription": "This app is built and maintained on my free time. Your support helps keep it alive and growing.",
  "changelogTitle": "What's new",
  "changelogGotIt": "Got it",
  "changelogV120I18n": "Multi-language: app interface in 26 languages, map labels in 41, date formats follow your locale. Override in Settings or the wizard.",
  "changelogV120Wizard": "First-launch wizard: pick your defaults (theme, language) and grant location permissions in one flow.",
  "changelogV120Recording": "Activity recording: animated location marker with pulse and accuracy circle, kilometre markers on the map, hold Stop for 3 seconds to end (no accidental taps), auto-redirect to stats.",
  "changelogV120Stats": "Activity stats: per-kilometre splits chart with pace ⇄ speed toggle, D+ elevation gain (matches Strava/Garmin convention).",
  "changelogV120Share": "Share an activity as a card with map and stats via the system share sheet.",
  "changelogV120GpxImport": "Import GPX files from other apps (Garmin, Strava, etc.) — both track and route points supported.",
  "changelogV120MapThemes": "Five map themes: Light, Dark, White, Grayscale, Black — pick the one that fits your eye in Settings.",
  "changelogV120Reproducible": "Reproducible builds: anyone can rebuild from source and verify the published APK is byte-for-byte identical — no hidden code, no tampering.",
  "changelogV120Stability": "Stability: hardened against junk GPS fixes, reliable background recording that resumes after the system kills the app, automatic log rotation, stricter GPX validation, HTTP timeouts.",
  "changelogV130LiveShare": "Live sharing: while recording, share an end-to-end encrypted link and let followers watch your position in their browser — no account on either side, the key never leaves the link.",
  "changelogV130Profiles": "Activity profiles: walk, run, ride, car, swim, aircraft or other — the choice sizes GPS sampling and accuracy tolerance, and is stored with the activity.",
  "changelogV130Map": "New map engine: zoom and pan are now rendered by MapLibre Native — the zoom sweep that used to stutter is now smooth.",
  "changelogV130Puck": "The location marker is now drawn by the app itself: a dot at a standstill, a chevron along your direction of travel, true-north compass on Android.",
  "changelogV130Detail": "Recording detail: pick precise, balanced or endurance GPS sampling to trade accuracy against battery per activity.",
  "changelogV130Left": "Left-handed mode: the map controls can move to the left side of the screen (Settings).",
  "changelogV130CarFix": "Fixed: a car above 126 km/h recorded nothing at all — the speed filter now adapts to each activity instead of rejecting every fix.",
  "changelogV140Offline": "Offline maps: keep the area around you — 10 to 100 km — so the map still works where there is no signal (Settings).",
  "changelogV140OfflineCost": "Each kept area says what it cost in tiles and megabytes, and one that was cut short says how far it got — ask for it again to finish it.",
  "changelogV140Cache": "The map you simply looked at is kept too, up to 1 GB, and can be thrown away on its own without touching the areas you chose to keep.",
  "changelogV140Drift": "Fixed: a phone left standing no longer piles up distance from GPS drift — a stationary recording now reads zero instead of inventing metres.",
  "changelogV140Elevation": "Fixed: elevation counts confirmed climbs instead of rounding every reading to ten metres, so small hills stop vanishing and flat ground stops gaining.",
  "changelogV140LocationOff": "When location services are switched off the map now says so and offers to open the setting, and tracking picks up again by itself once they return.",
  "changelogV140Markers": "Distance markers along a route can be set to the spacing you want, or turned off (Settings).",
  "changelogV140Stop": "Stopping a recording draws its hold progress above your thumb instead of under it, so you can see how much longer to hold.",
  "changelogV140SmallScreens": "Fixed: the setup steps and the settings screens stay usable on short and compact screens.",
